														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3597442">
									

<p>It's pleasant, but I'm not sure if this is the right place for it.</p>
<p><strong>EDIT:</strong> Actually, fuck it, I'll elaborate.</p>
<p>What place does this have on the SCP wiki? As far as I can tell, it's some kind of meta self-indulgence between you and your own character. Okay? My issue is that unlike something like <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3999">3999</a>, for example, which takes on the battle between creator and creation in an interesting and engaging way, this instead just provides us with a short and fairly empty resolution to a problem I don't think many people can relate to. You're worried about writing happy things? Why? 'Happy' skips have been around since the very beginning (<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-999">SCP-999</a> and <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-348">SCP-348</a> spring to mind), and are in fact amongst some of the most popular skips on the site. You can't die on a hill when there's no hill to die on.</p>
<p>I don't know, even ignoring the subject matter the writing itself isn't exactly spectacular. There's a whole lot of pointless nothing for the majority of the first sequence (the phone thing and the sock tangent struck me as a bit weird- I get that it's supposed to add character but it just feels detached and out of place), followed by a very jarring switch into this meta strangeness that feels too petty to even be considered a 'conflict' in the first place. In every line of it.</p>
<p>Maybe I'm entirely missing something, and if so, please point it out to me- I <em>want</em> to like this, but I'm scratching my head trying to figure out what the point of it is. Can this even be considered a tale? I was under the impression that SCP tales had to be about&#8230; you know, SCP stuff. This is just generic feel-good fluff that envokes very little emotion. You wrote something nice, sure- but posting it on the main site unfortunately feels less about the literary goal and more about just getting it out there.</p>
<p><strong>EDIT x2:</strong> I only just realised what the last line meant- is this <em>really</em> suggesting that they wiped their attempt at a sad skip and replaced it with a <em>heart</em>? That's Disney Channel levels of corny.<br />
I'm sorry, really, but none of this works for me.</p>
<p>-1</p>

