<p>Hence why the conversation happens between me and my author avatar, it's not meant to include anyone else.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Then that begs the question- why write an entire tale based around something so minor? It comes across as arrogance, pulling what even you admit to be a downtrodden niggle into something with more weight than it deserves.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>things like what exact document is being worked on, the music playing, the fact that Chibi's socks don't match, or the exact time of the moment don't actually have meaning unless given meaning to them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That concept isn't integrated well enough to be successful, I feel? It does come across as random extraneous details with no relevance to the story. That is a weakness of the writing. Telling me what the <em>intentions</em> of it were doesn't alter that perspective.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>character and creator don't have an antagonistic relationship.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If there's no conflict within the story, what is there at stake? Why should I care or even feel invested? That makes this the equivalent of a motivational quote. Again, sorry to repeat myself, but it feels very self-indulgent to a degree at which I can't take the message seriously.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The &quot;&lt;3&quot; Chibi leaves is one last message in response to that bit of &quot;kindness&quot; so to speak.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That doesn't excuse it from coming across as a bit childish.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>Please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
<p>Clearly people like it- so maybe I'm too thick or too cold-hearted to care for it myself- but the article feels like dead weight that boils down to a bog-standard 'write what you want to write' message- something that I don't think as many people take so personally- and it overwhelms whatever other intentions you may have had. Hell, I've wanted to break away from my comfort zone and failed miserably. I don't think it's worth writing a strange tale about in which I converse with my self-insert. It's not my cup of tea- so I'm staying firm with my downvote.</p>

							</div>

								
