															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1436137&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609233410" alt="fieldstone" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1436137)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;" >fieldstone</a></span> <span class="odate time_1505856286 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Sep 2017 21:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3597645">
									

<p>I agree with bittermixin about this being out of place here. I haven't downvoted it solely because it's written so intimately that doing so would actually feel rude. The narrator-conversing-with-author-avatar format is really, really not my thing, but I'm open to it - however, nothing much happens here, making it read less like a story and more like a journal entry or blog post.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;and&nbsp;I&nbsp;found&nbsp;I&nbsp;had&nbsp;more&nbsp;to&nbsp;say</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Thematically, this is weird to me. I very rarely think &quot;I need less darkness and misery in my entertainment,&quot; but when I do, I just go to another site for a while, or draw/write/play something that's not SCP-related. The central conflict here just isn't clicking for me &#8212; it's like going to a concert and then wondering why things have to be so loud all the time.</p>
<p>To go another level deeper into that line of thought, I don't necessarily agree that the SCP world is all misery anyway; lots of bad stuff happens, sure, but the fantasy at the heart of it all is <em>we have the means to take control of our world</em>, and I don't see that as inherently pessimistic at all. As a whole, this site tells the story of humanity facing a senseless, hostile universe and saying &quot;well, fuck you too, then,&quot; and mostly making it work. I might just be a twisted person, but that's inspiring to me, not depressing.</p>
<p>It's a nice warm piece of writing, but the fact that it's delivered through the mainlist puts me off; in the end, &quot;I have very mixed feelings about this&quot; still counts as conveying an emotion, so that's something. I'm surprised by the general acceptance this is getting &#8212; more power to ya, but I really wouldn't want to see this become a trend.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

